<title>FRANCE: Lagardere, Thomson stock delayed.</title>
<headline>Lagardere, Thomson stock delayed.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in Lagardere, Thomson SA and Thomson-CSF was delayed at the opening of the Paris bourse on Wednesday after the government said it preferred an offer by Lagardere for Thomson, the SBF bourse association said.</p>
<p>A spokesman could not give a time for the shares to resume trading.</p>
<p>Lagardere shares closed on Tuesday at 133.1 francs. Shares in state-controlled Thomson SA closed at 975 francs. Thomson-CSF closed at 161.20 francs.  </p>
<p>Lagardere has submitted a bid to buy state electronics group Thomson in competition with Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>The government said on Wednesday it preferred Lagardere's offer but would make a final decision after a study by the state privatisation body.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
